<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices rose final 0.2 pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices rose final 0.2 pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following final data:</p>
<p>				    Feb	  Jan	Feb 1996</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation   0.2	  0.3	  0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation     1.6	  1.8	  2.0</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)    114.9	114.7	113.1</p>
<p>				    Feb   Last 3 months   yr/yr</p>
<p> EU harmonised inflation*   0.3	  0.7	  1.7</p>
<p>EU harmonised inflation index</p>
<p>				    Feb 97    Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>				    101.0     100.7	99.3</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the traditional French consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990 (not EU harmonised).</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.20    108.2  -0.8    1.1    1.5</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  32.77    108.4   0.9   -0.1    0.5</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.64    125.9   0.2    0.6    1.7</p>
<p> Energy				8.66    115.7  -0.1    1.0    5.3</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.46    130.0   0.4    3.0    2.5</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.68    130.2   0.2    0.5    2.0</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.59    110.0  -0.1   -0.1    0.6</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.02    113.8   0.2    0.4    1.4</p>
<p>NOTE - European Union harmonised data complies with definitions in the Maastricht treaty and is meant to allow comparisons between member states. Harmonised inflation data across the EU was first published earlier this month for the month of January.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
